    "episodeSummary": "A 34-year-old female with a history of similar self-terminating episodes presented with palpitations. Vitals showed a heart rate of 190 bpm, stable blood pressure (118/76 mmHg), and normal oxygen saturation (98%). ECG revealed a regular narrow-complex tachycardia with a ventricular rate of 190 bpm, no clear P waves, and no ST deviation. Electrolytes (potassium, magnesium) were within normal limits. Troponin was negative. The episode was captured and classified as stable supraventricular tachycardia.",
